+## v35 durable obtained flags and Endless mode
+
+Storage checks cover recovery from photo history with a missing older ledger,
+checked-by-default finds, uncheck/recheck across independent connections and
+restart, idempotent UI/photo replays, deleted photos/history, entries within
+the photo cooldown, and 16:00 day boundaries. A child process commits a find
+and exits immediately with os._exit, without running UI or shutdown callbacks;
+a new process connection still reads the find, metadata and count.
+
+Production-runner checks cover Endless starts at 4/5, 5/5 and 6/5, continuing
+after collection/home return, F10 staying stopped, turning Endless off to
+restore normal quota, and unchecking a fifth find during collection. Existing
+fifth-find-across-reset, exact return, no sixth find in normal mode, map and
+cursor protections remain covered. The repeat-loop fixture uses the same two
+OpenCV threads as the application and a 15-second bounded join, with cleanup
+on timeout, to avoid failing valid virtual-clock loops on a busy test host.
+
+Windows Sniper integration launches the actual Tk app twice on the same
+isolated profile. It toggles Obtained off/on/off, retains the original photo,
+reopens the app to restore 4/5 and Endless enabled, checks Obtained again,
+then scans beyond 5/5 until F10. Turning Endless off restores the start guard.
+Native source/frozen GUI checks verify the checkbox position under Gems found
+and the daily-history UI. Packaging requires the new native report fields.
+The full Windows suite, native input, source/frozen resources and complete 7z
+round-trip checks are required. This is not a live BlueStacks game test.
